Description: frontend: scenes and the preview in the canvas's scene space; displays named for a module
 The preview, studio mode's program view, the projectors, the multiview, item alignment, dropped files and the
 spacing helpers lay out in the main canvas's scene space (one eye of a side by side canvas, obs_get_video_eye_size()),
 so a scene item placed at 100 px is at 100 eye samples in both eyes, and a display one eye wide holds the left eye
 whole, never two squeezed eyes. Each display widget carries its obs_display as the property "obsDisplay" (0 while it
 has none), for a module that shows it as a 3D area. The output and the encoders keep the canvas's whole size.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 61, milestone 3)
Forwarded: no, OBS asks for human-written submissions only (CONTRIBUTING.md, AI/Machine Learning Policy)
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
